WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
Consider a payment rule: negative amounts
must be rejected without changing balances

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.200
or the ledger. The target workflow
starts with that domain-owned contract.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:15.200
A bounded generator proposes a test,
independent execution challenges it,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.080
and a reviewer decides through
existing release controls.

00:00:18.272 --> 00:00:22.000
Failures become new cases.
This is an illustrative

00:00:22.053 --> 00:00:26.080
workflow to validate with the bank.
Shared services support the proof,

00:00:26.093 --> 00:00:28.640
while the payment owner retains
the meaning of correctness.
